{
  "id": "ss.relic.movespeed",
  "name": "Cricket leg",
  "description": "The back leg of a cricket, folded the way it waits: a broad femur banded across the grain, a thin tibia falling away from the knee at a hard angle, four curved spines hooking back off its outer edge and the tarsus still on the end. Dark carapace rather than bright chitin \u2014 this came off the ruins, not off a living thing. Polish: the tibia's ink underlay was a fraction of a pixel wider than the tibia itself and the spines had none, so both now sit on real ink; the spines and the tarsus are two pixels thick, the tibia is lifted one step so it separates from its own outline, and the femur bands are a touch heavier. The pose is unchanged. Says pass: a leg folded the way it waits said the opposite of the stat it carries \u2014 and the line about it having come off something that had stopped moving was the drawing arguing with its own slot. Three streaks off the back of the stroke put it in motion. Same leg, now drawn doing the one thing it is on the plate for.",
  "tags": ["relic"],
  "says": ["faster"],
  "size": [32, 32],
